Kestrel Shaders @VERSION@ - setup
================================

This folder sets up everything for the official Minecraft Launcher in one go:
Fabric for Minecraft @MC_VERSION@, Sodium and Iris (downloaded from Modrinth, checksums
checked), and Kestrel Shaders, switched on with the quality profile you choose. It adds a
new "Kestrel Shaders" installation with its own game folder, so your other installations,
mods and worlds are left alone.

Before you start
----------------
- Install the Minecraft Launcher, start it once, log in, then QUIT it.
- You need an internet connection while the installer runs.

Mac (M1 Mac mini and other Macs)
--------------------------------
1. Double-click "Install on Mac.command".
   If macOS won't open it ("unidentified developer"), use Terminal instead, which always
   works: open Terminal, type  bash  and a space, drag "Install on Mac.command" into the
   Terminal window, and press Return.
2. Press Return to accept the suggested profile (MEDIUM on Apple Silicon).
3. Open the Minecraft Launcher, pick "Kestrel Shaders", press Play.

For the best frame rate on a Mac mini with a 4K screen, set the display to a "1x" mode
first (System Settings > Displays).

Windows
-------
1. Double-click "Install on Windows.bat".
   If Windows SmartScreen appears: More info > Run anyway.
2. Press Enter for LOW, or type 1-4 for another profile.
3. Open the Minecraft Launcher, pick "Kestrel Shaders", press Play.

Afterwards
----------
- The first start downloads Minecraft @MC_VERSION@ and Fabric; give it a minute.
- If Iris says it can't run with Vulkan, accept the switch to OpenGL. The game closes;
  start it again.
- Change the profile in game: press I (or Options > Video Settings > Shader Packs).
- Your worlds: the new installation has its own "saves" folder (the installer prints where).
  Copy a world into it to play that world with the shaders.
- Run the installer again any time to update Fabric, Sodium and Iris.

Using the Modrinth App or Prism Launcher instead?
-------------------------------------------------
Create a Fabric @MC_VERSION@ instance, add Iris (it brings Sodium), and copy
@PACK@ into the instance's "shaderpacks" folder. Then pick Kestrel Shaders in
Options > Video Settings > Shader Packs.
